      },
      "text": "#Vault7 linked #Longhorn group infiltrated governments, international orgs, other targets The link to Vault 7 A number of documents disclosed by WikiLeaks outline specifications and requirements for malware tools.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_8",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Symantec_Longhorn-Tools(04-10-2017)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p1_s8"
      },
      "text": "One document is a development timeline for a piece of malware called Fluxwire, containing a changelog of dates for when new features were incorporated.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_9",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Symantec_Longhorn-Tools(04-10-2017)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s1"
      },
      "text": "dates align closely with the development of one Longhorn tool (Trojan.Corentry) tracked by Symantec.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_10",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Symantec_Longhorn-Tools(04-10-2017)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s2"
      },
      "text": "New features in Corentry consistently appeared in samples obtained by Symantec either on the same date listed in the Vault 7 document or several days later, leaving little doubt that Corentry is the malware described in the leaked document.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_11",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Symantec_Longhorn-Tools(04-10-2017)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s3"
      },
      "text": "Early versions of Corentry seen by Symantec contained a reference to the file path for the Fluxwire program database (PDB) file.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_13",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Symantec_Longhorn-Tools(04-10-2017)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s5"
      },
      "text": "The specification of the payload and the interface used to load it was closely matched in another Longhorn tool called Backdoor.Plexor.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_19",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Symantec_Longhorn-Tools(04-10-2017)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 3,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p3_s5"
      },
      "text": "Global reach: Longhorn’s operations While active since at least 2011, with some evidence of activity dating back as far as 2007, Longhorn first came to Symantec’s attention in 2014 with the use of a zero-day exploit (CVE- 2014-4148) embedded in a Word document to infect a target with Plexor.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_22",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Symantec_Longhorn-Tools(04-10-2017)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 3,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p3_s8"
      },
      "text": "Symantec has seen Longhorn use four different malware tools against its targets: Corentry, Plexor, Backdoor.Trojan.LH1, and Backdoor.Trojan.LH2.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_36",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Symantec_Longhorn-Tools(04-10-2017)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 4,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p4_s4"
      },
      "text": "The acronym MTWRFSU (Monday Tuesday Wednesday ThuRsday Friday Saturday SUnday) was used to configure which day of the week malware would communicate with the attackers.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_38",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Symantec_Longhorn-Tools(04-10-2017)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 4,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p4_s6"
      },
      "text": "Distinctive fingerprints Longhorn has used advanced malware tools and zero-day vulnerabilities to infiltrate a string of targets worldwide.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_39",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Symantec_Longhorn-Tools(04-10-2017)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 4,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p4_s7"
      },
      "text": "Taken in combination, the tools, techniques, and procedures employed by Longhorn are distinctive and unique to this group, leaving little doubt about its link to Vault 7.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
